Bug 1991785 - Stop the calendar from dropping a saved login the server never rejected. r=arschmitz,mkmelin

The prompt deleted a saved login whenever it had handed the same one out
twice within a minute, guessing that a second challenge meant the password
was wrong. It means nothing of the sort - requests that go out before
anything has authenticated are each challenged. A server log caught it:
three uploads inside one second, no credentials on any of them, none
rejected, and the login gone afterwards. Address books share the entry, so
they lose it too.

Ask PREVIOUS_FAILED instead, and drop only what we handed out ourselves.

The removal branch also returned an object where its callers read a boolean,
so it reported success without supplying credentials and no dialog appeared.

The username is now set on the auth info even when no login was found, so
the dialog names the account it asks for instead of showing an empty field.
That is what bug 1994131 and bug 2004690 ask for.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319397

